---
// Catalogue entry. Dutch mirror: ./nl/index.astro (edit both together).
import CataloguePage from "../../components/hall/CataloguePage.astro";
const wip = "/images/puzzle-quests/skeleton-key-wip";
---
<CataloguePage
  lang="en"
  path="/puzzlequests/"
  title="Puzzle Quests | The Lions Alliance"
  description="Hand-built walking quests for museums and heritage venues, carried by a physical prop instead of an app. Skeleton Key is first, in build and testing with Museum Medelo in Meijel."
  crumb="Walking quests"
  h1="Puzzle Quests"
  facts={[
    ["Object", "Walking quest with a hand-built prop"],
    ["First quest", "Skeleton Key: De Vlucht door de Peel"],
    ["Route", "Meijel, about 5 km, eight hidden lock-stations"],
    ["Venue", "Museum Medelo, Tomveld 2, Meijel"],
    ["Partner", "Heemkundevereniging Medelo"],
    ["Status", "In build and testing; trail run next"],
  ]}
  lede="A local legend, discovered on foot. Visitors carry a hand-built key out of the museum and along a route through the landscape. No app, no screen, no host needed."
  plate={{
    src: `${wip}/IMG20260901145952.webp`, w: 1600, h: 1200, vt: "exhibit-key",
    alt: "The Skeleton Key in build: a 3D-printed key with a lion's head and a clear shaft for eight lights, on a green workbench mat",
    caption: "The Skeleton Key in build, before its brass finish. The clear shaft holds the eight lights.",
  }}
  cta={{ href: "/contact/", label: "Enquire about a quest" }}
  link={{ href: "#quest", label: "Read the quest" }}
>
  <section class="cat-section">
    <h2>The legend behind the route</h2>
    <p>Skeleton Key is built around a real Meijel legend. In the 1730s, young men fled Prussian recruiters through the Peel, using a network of hidden safe-houses. Visitors carry a hand-built brass key that sends them out to find that escape route for themselves. The key leaves the museum desk with them and grows more insistent as they near each hidden station, until the story is complete and they return with their answer.</p>
    <p>It is being built with <strong>Heemkundevereniging Medelo</strong>, the local-history society behind Museum Medelo, the same museum where Medelotapps and Brief aan Jan Truijen run. Skeleton Key is the first of three quests planned for the site. Once it is proven with real players, the same hardware and format carry over to Living Chronicle and Puzzle Lantern, and later to other venues.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section">
    <h2>What a group does</h2>
    <ol class="cat-steps">
      <li><div><strong>Collect the kit</strong><span>At the museum desk: the key, a booklet, a route sheet and a short briefing in the story. No app, no screen, no setup.</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Walk the route</strong><span>Through the village and the landscape around it. The key responds at every station and gives one more piece of the story.</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Return to the desk</strong><span>With a completed booklet and the key lit up with their progress. Staff check it, stamp the sheet and share one extra detail from the archive. The kit is ready for the next group in under five minutes.</span></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section" id="quest">
    <h2>The quests</h2>
    <div class="cat-sub">
      <h3>De Vlucht door de Peel <span class="tla-badge tla-badge--dev">In build and testing</span></h3>
      <dl class="cat-table">
        <dt>Difficulty</dt><dd>3 of 4</dd>
        <dt>Duration</dt><dd>75&ndash;95 minutes</dd>
        <dt>Distance</dt><dd>About 5 km</dd>
        <dt>Group</dt><dd>2&ndash;6 people, age 10 and up</dd>
        <dt>Mechanic</dt><dd>A chain of locks, sensed by radio</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="cat-sub__story">Between 1713 and 1740, Prussian King Frederick Wilhelm I sent recruiters across the border to collect exceptionally tall young men for his elite Riesengarde. The men who fled used a secret network of safe-houses through the Peel. Those who made it to Meijel were free. They settled, married and had tall children. This is documented as the reason Meijel has historically had more tall men than its neighbouring villages.</p>
      <p>The Skeleton Key is the warden&rsquo;s master pass. Eight lock-stations are hidden in tree trunks, mossy stones and trail posts along the route, invisible to a casual passer-by. Each one pulses with light when the key senses it. At each lock the key is turned, an NFC scan triggers, and one more rune along its shaft glows through the aged brass. At the final lock all eight are lit, and the walker speaks the answer aloud at the museum desk as proof of the journey.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-sub">
      <h3>Living Chronicle: Het Pad van Dikke Mie <span class="tla-badge tla-badge--future">Planned</span></h3>
      <p>A self-writing leather chronicle that fills in as you walk a memorial route for a forgotten 18th-century vagrant. The prop is built once Skeleton Key&rsquo;s trail run has proven the format.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-sub">
      <h3>Puzzle Lantern: De Schat van het Dolle Moer <span class="tla-badge tla-badge--future">Planned</span></h3>
      <p>A Victorian-style lantern that reveals UV-hidden clues at each station, decoded against a field journal. Same story family, after Skeleton Key in the build queue.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section" id="venue">
    <h2>The hardware is reusable. The story is the work.</h2>
    <div class="cat-lists">
      <div>
        <h3>What stays the same</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The prop hardware.</li>
          <li>The puzzle framework.</li>
          <li>How the desk runs it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What we make for your venue</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The story.</li>
          <li>The booklet.</li>
          <li>The route.</li>
          <li>How the stations are disguised.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="plates">
    <figure class="cat-plate cat-plate--wide">
      <img src={`${wip}/IMG20260608130746.webp`} width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="The Skeleton Key workbench mid-build: tools, electronics and parts bins" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 2.</b> The workbench, mid-build. Still very much in progress.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="cat-plate">
      <img src={`${wip}/IMG20260608105918.webp`} width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="A small controller board with connectors, held in helping hands on the workbench" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 3.</b> Electronics for the key, soldered by hand.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="enquiry">
    <div class="cat-enquiry__grid">
      <div>
        <h2>A quest for your museum or village</h2>
        <p>Tell us about your place and the story it holds. We reply within one or two working days.</p>
        <div class="cat-enquiry__actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="tla-btn">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-enquiry__for">
        Made for
        <ul>
          <li>Regional and local-history museums</li>
          <li>Heritage societies</li>
          <li>Campsites and heritage routes</li>
          <li>Tourism organisations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CataloguePage>
